Package: contentvalidR
Type: Package
Title: Tools for Substantive and Content Validity Pretesting
Version: 0.1.0.9000
Authors@R: c(
    person(given = "Joshua", family = "Uhalt", email = "Josh.Uhalt@gmail.com",
           role = c("aut", "cre"))
    )
Description: Provides quantitative tools for substantive and content-oriented
    scale pretesting. Implements item-sort indices from Anderson and Gerbing
    (1991), exact item-sort inference following Howard and Melloy (2016),
    empirical interpretation benchmarks from Colquitt et al. (2019),
    the Hinkin and Tracey (1999) construct-rating procedure with HTC/HTD
    indices and repeated-measures item screening, and
    an expert-panel workflow combining Aiken's V with score confidence intervals,
    Lawshe content validity ratios with exact inference, content validity indices
    with modified kappa, and item-objective congruence.
    User-facing workflows emphasize interpretable summaries and transparent
    review recommendations rather than isolated coefficients.
